    {
      "id": "p0050-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "When Undertale debuted in English in September 2015, it wasn't locked to a single region - gamers anywhere in the world could purchase it. The game was only available in English, however, and could only be played on home computers. This language barrier, coupled with the need for a computer, made the gam inaccessible for most Japanese gamers. As a result, Undertale experienced a very different \"release history\" in Japan that can be divided into three distinct stages.",
        "raw": "When Under tale debuted in English in September 2015, it wasn't locked to a\nsingle region - gamers anywhere in the world could purchase it. The game was\nonly available in English, however, and could only be played on home computers.\nThis language barrier, coupled with the need for a computer, made the gam\ninaccessible for most Japanese gamers. As a result, Undertale experienced a very\ndifferent \"release history\" in Japan that can be divided into three distinct stages.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2862073,
          0.09147143,
          0.89282027,
          0.20460714
        ],
