    {
      "id": "p0050-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Although this unofficial translation made the game playable in Japanese, other barriers stood in the way. First, the vast majority of Japanese gamers at the time relied on mainstream gaming systems or mobile devices to play games, not home computers. Players would also need to be savvy enough to buy the original game from English-language websites, download the translation patch from elsewhere, decompress the files, apply the patch successfully, and deal with any technical issues along the way. Thus Undertale remained inaccessible to most Japanese gamers.",
        "raw": "Although this unofficial translation made the game playable in Japanese, other\nbarriers stood in the way. First, the vast majority of Japanese gamers at the\ntime relied on mainstream gaming systems or mobile devices to play games,\nnot home computers. Players would also need to be savvy enough to buy the\noriginal game from English-language websites, download the translation patch\nfrom elsewhere, decompress the files, apply the patch successfully, and deal\nwith any technical issues along the way. Thus Undertale remained inaccessible\nto most Japanese gamers.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28765801,
          0.75995,
          0.89402751,
          0.90245
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28417832,
          0.75923571,
          0.89605648,
          0.90352143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          59,
          60,
          61,
          62,
          63,
          64,
          65,
          66
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "虽然非官方译版让游戏能用日语玩，其他障碍仍在。首先，当时绝大多数日本玩家用主流游戏主机或移动设备玩游戏，而不是个人电脑。玩家还得有足够的技术知识：到英语网站购买原版，从别处下载翻译补丁，解压文件，成功打上补丁，并解决沿途可能出现的技术问题。因此，多数日本玩家依然难以接触 Undertale。",
        "status": "draft",
